{title: Joy to the World (FJ_14_en)}
{song_number: 14}
{language: en}
{key: D}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[D]Joy to the world, the [G]Lord is [D/A]come! [A]Let [D]earth re[G]ceive her [A]King;
[D]let every heart prepare Him room, and Heaven and nature sing,
and [A]Heaven and nature [D]sing, and [G]Heaven, and [D]Heaven and [A]nature [D]sing.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[D]Joy to the earth, the [G]Saviour [D/A]reigns! [A]Let [D]men their [G]songs em[A]ploy;
[D]while fields and floods, rocks, hills and plains repeat the sounding joy,
re[A]peat the sounding [D]joy, re[G]peat, re[D]peat the [A]sounding [D]joy.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[D]No more let sins and sorrow grow, nor thorns infest the ground;
He comes to make His blessings flow far as the curse is found,
far [A]as the curse is [D]found, far [G]as, far [D]as the [A]curse is [D]found.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
[D]He rules the world with truth and grace, and makes the nations prove
the glories of His righteousness, and wonders of His love,
and [A]wonders of His [D]love, and [G]wonders, [D]wonders [A]of His [D]love.
{end_of_verse}
